## 11. Cost Recovery

You may request or collect payment solely to recover reasonable and good-faith direct costs incurred in distributing or operating access to the Software.

Permitted direct costs may include:

* server costs;
* bandwidth;
* storage;
* domain registration;
* build infrastructure;
* code-signing costs;
* payment-processing costs;
* physical media;
* packaging;
* shipping; and
* substantially similar direct distribution expenses.

Cost Recovery must:

1. be reasonably related to actual costs;
2. not contain a material profit margin; and
3. not be structured primarily as a method of monetizing access to the Software.

General business profit, development profit, licensing profit, scarcity premiums, or arbitrary access fees do not qualify as Cost Recovery.

Voluntary donations may be requested separately from Cost Recovery.

