## 16. Access Information

"Access Information" means information whose principal practical purpose is enabling a person to locate, identify, unlock, retrieve, download, or obtain the Software.

Access Information may include:

* URLs;
* repository addresses;
* mirror addresses;
* file-hosting addresses;
* package locations;
* download identifiers;
* download tokens;
* passwords;
* access codes;
* invitation codes;
* decryption credentials;
* torrent identifiers;
* magnet URIs;
* QR codes;
* file identifiers;
* API endpoints;
* retrieval commands; and
* substantially similar information.

Information does not become Access Information merely because it discusses, describes, reviews, teaches, analyzes, or refers to the Software.

Tutorials, journalism, reviews, commentary, research, documentation, books, educational material, and substantive media remain covered by the Media permission.

A monetized article, video, livestream, tutorial, or other substantive publication may include Access Information incidentally, provided payment is not specifically required to reveal or obtain that Access Information.

For example:

* a monetized YouTube video may freely include the Original Repository link in its description;
* an advertisement-supported article may provide a direct download link;
* a sponsored tutorial may provide a free repository link;
* a paid book may mention the publicly available repository as part of substantive educational content.

Those activities are permitted.

