## 17. Nature of Commercial Restrictions

The Commercial Exploitation restrictions operate as conditions on permissions granted under this license to the extent that the relevant activity requires permission from the Licensor under applicable intellectual-property law.

For persons who accept these terms, those restrictions may also operate as contractual obligations to the extent permitted by applicable law.

Nothing in these terms claims copyright, ownership, or another exclusive intellectual-property right in:

* facts;
* URLs;
* addresses;
* identifiers;
* publicly known locations;
* ordinary instructions; or
* other material that applicable law does not protect merely because it constitutes Access Information.

Nothing in this license creates an exclusive intellectual-property right where applicable law does not provide one.

---

## 18. Monetized Redirects and Download Intermediation

You may not commercially monetize the act of directing a person to the Software where access is conditioned on passing through a monetized intermediary.

Prohibited arrangements include requiring users to pass through:

* paid URL shorteners;
* advertising shorteners;
* offer walls;
* affiliate redirects;
* sponsored redirects;
* mandatory intermediate advertising pages;
* paid download gateways;
* monetized redirect chains; or
* substantially similar intermediaries

before receiving the actual download or Access Information.

You may operate an advertising-supported website or mirror provided that the legitimate download remains directly accessible without mandatory advertising interaction.

---

## 19. No Artificial Scarcity

You may not intentionally create artificial scarcity around otherwise available copies or Access Information primarily for commercial monetization.

For example, you may not commercially charge for:

* an intentionally hidden public download link;
* an intentionally hidden repository address;
* a password created primarily to monetize access;
* a private mirror created primarily to sell access to an otherwise freely available release;
* a paid membership role whose principal benefit is obtaining the Software; or
* access intentionally withheld from the public primarily to create a paid access tier.

This section does not prohibit:

* genuine private development;
* unreleased development builds;
* private testing versions;
* commissioned work that does not itself violate the Commercial Exploitation provisions;
* security embargoes;
* staged technical testing;
* legitimate release scheduling; or
* temporary restricted access for non-commercial operational reasons.

