## 21. Licensed Components

"Licensed Components" means the source code, code, scripts, assets, documentation, configuration, or other copyrightable material originally offered by the Licensor under this license.

A file or component remains a Licensed Component when incorporated into a larger application, archive, package, executable, repository, container, or other combined work.

---

## 22. Covered Modifications

"Covered Modifications" means material that directly modifies or derives from Licensed Components.

Covered Modifications include:

* edits to Licensed Components;
* modified copies of Licensed Components;
* translated Licensed Components;
* adapted Licensed Components;
* code copied from Licensed Components and subsequently modified;
* material substantially derived from Licensed Components; and
* replacement material created by directly adapting the expression or implementation of Licensed Components.

A newly created component does not become a Covered Modification merely because it:

* interoperates with the Software;
* depends on the Software;
* calls the Software;
* imports the Software;
* links to the Software;
* loads the Software;
* implements an interface used by the Software;
* provides an interface used by the Software; or
* is designed specifically to work with the Software.

---

## 23. Independent Components

"Independent Component" means material that:

1. was independently authored or lawfully obtained;
2. does not contain a substantial portion of Licensed Components;
3. is not itself a direct modification or adaptation of Licensed Components; and
4. remains reasonably identifiable as independently authored material.

Independent Components may be distributed under any terms chosen by their respective copyright holders.

Such terms may include:

* MIT;
* BSD;
* Apache;
* GPL;
* LGPL;
* MPL;
* another free-software license;
* another open-source license;
* another source-available license;
* a custom license; or
* proprietary and closed-source terms.

Nothing in this license requires disclosure of the source code of Independent Components.

---

## 24. Source Preservation

You may not convert Distributed Licensed Components or Covered Modifications into closed-source material.

Whenever you Distribute Licensed Components or Covered Modifications in:

* executable form;
* binary form;
* compiled form;
* bytecode;
* minified form;
* obfuscated form;
* packaged form;
* generated form; or
* another form that is not reasonably suitable for modification,

you must also make the corresponding source code of those Licensed Components and Covered Modifications available as required by these terms.

This requirement applies only to Licensed Components and Covered Modifications.

It does not extend to Independent Components.

---

## 25. No Viral Licensing

This license is intentionally non-viral.

The licensing conditions applicable to Licensed Components and Covered Modifications do not automatically extend to independently authored code merely because the code is combined with or interacts with the Software.

You are not required to license an entire:

* project;
* repository;
* application;
* executable;
* package;
* installer;
* container;
* service;
* library;
* operating environment; or
* Larger Work

under this license merely because Licensed Components are present.

Only Licensed Components and Covered Modifications remain subject to this license's Source Preservation requirements.

---

## 26. Linking and Integration Exception

An Independent Component does not become subject to this license merely because it:

* statically links to the Software;
* dynamically links to the Software;
* imports the Software;
* loads the Software as a library;
* calls functions supplied by the Software;
* exposes functions to the Software;
* uses a plugin interface;
* implements a plugin interface;
* uses an extension interface;
* calls an API;
* exposes an API;
* communicates through IPC;
* communicates through sockets;
* communicates through shared memory;
* communicates through pipes;
* communicates through HTTP;
* communicates through another network protocol;
* invokes the Software as a separate process;
* exchanges files with the Software;
* exchanges structured data with the Software;
* shares a database with the Software;
* is compiled into the same executable;
* is packaged into the same application;
* is distributed in the same archive;
* is distributed by the same installer;
* appears in the same repository;
* runs in the same container;
* runs on the same computer; or
* otherwise interoperates with the Software.

This exception applies even when the Independent Component is proprietary or closed source.

