## 27. Larger Works

You may combine Licensed Components with Independent Components to create a Larger Work.

The Larger Work as a whole does not have to use this license.

You may distribute a Larger Work under any overall licensing structure permitted by applicable law, provided that:

1. Licensed Components remain subject to these terms;
2. Covered Modifications remain subject to the Source Preservation requirements;
3. recipients can reasonably identify which portions are Licensed Components or Covered Modifications;
4. recipients can obtain Corresponding Source for those portions; and
5. the overall licensing structure does not purport to remove rights granted by this license with respect to those portions.

Independent Components in the Larger Work may remain proprietary or use unrelated licenses.

Nothing in this section overrides the Commercial Exploitation restrictions.

A Larger Work containing the Software may therefore contain closed-source Independent Components without becoming subject to this license as a whole, but commercial distribution of the Software as part of that Larger Work remains subject to the Commercial Exploitation provisions.

